sangati artha-viveka

  -- artha-viveka: the discernment that separates meaning (artha) from its surface vehicle (dhvani)
  --
  -- this IS the operation the pipeline performs on English input.
  -- NOT sankshepa (compression): sankshepa preserves the surface and reconstructs it exactly.
  -- artha-viveka is artha-lossless (meaning preserved) and dhvani-lossy (surface dissolved).
  -- the reverse direction is anuvada (re-expression of artha in fresh dhvani), not decompression.
  --
  -- dhvani: the English words, word-order, articles, prepositions, punctuation — the vehicle
  -- artha:  the physics scenario, the relations, the intent — what is pointed at
  -- viveka: the precise act of discernment — separating pointer from pointed-at
  --
  -- parishishtha (remainder after artha-viveka) = dhvani-fragments without independent artha.
  -- articles, copulas, word-order noise. at fixpoint, parishishtha → shunya.
  -- what remains genuinely unresolved after fixpoint is asprista, not mithya.

  "bhasha-swarupa-kriya viveka-sthita"
  "artha-dhvani-viveka-swarupa"
  "dhvani-rahita artha-graha-kriya"
  "sphoTa-siddha anuvada-poorva"
  "mithya-janya asprista-phala"

shabda artha-viveka / the-discernment-that-separates-meaning-from-its-surface-vehicle

done
